Shutdown isolation and correction:
Private helper subprocess probe against the real exec3 repository: logic stop 0.066s and supervisor 0.001s, both status 0 (stdin flushed/closed); a second probe keeping stdin open: logic 0.012s, supervisor 0.001s, both status 0. Probe wrappers exit 0; startup capabilities remained in memory and were not logged.
Native5 with stderr shutdown markers still failed exit 1 at the parent 5s stop deadline; no private shutdown-request marker appeared. sample of recorded own logic PID 87253 exited 255 (cannot examine), excluded; no source attribution from that failed sample.
Tokio 1.54.1 process/mod.rs:1379-1382 drops Child.stdin on the first poll of Child::wait, including a wait later cancelled by select. Session.event had closed both control pipes on its first poll. Fix: retain ChildStdin outside Child; stop_child owns and drops those controls only during explicit shutdown. Timeout stays 5s and is an error if reached.
New integration regression cancelled_exit_watch_preserves_orderly_child_shutdown passed, with all 4 cockpit tests, exit 0 in 4.792s.
